## What to deliver

Build and rig the foundry up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a tall masonry tower with a throat up its center,
a stamping press riding in that throat, and a toothed drive gear on its flank. **Author
the two required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands:
`piston_stamp` (a weighty hammer that drives the press straight down to the bottom of
its stroke and eases back up, with weight — not a weightless linear slide) and
`gear_spin` (a steady full revolution that loops seamlessly). Both are self-playing and
looping, so the foundry runs on its own with no caller. The animations are the fixed
contract — produce both, by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are
yours. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your
finished submission.
